  "relations": [],
  "revisions": [
    {
      "clauses": [
        {
          "id": "clause:dcf5afb67b7c42faa04cf9ec24b8a798",
          "offset": 2,
          "overlaps": [],
          "parent_sha256": "9181921d4a1e05c3a62083c6243b1fdc8ab65446b6eabc52d2f73aaea1fd9394",
          "sha256": "8ced2565966d404c531140a6c3fa027b3633f8f1810d7dd4dfe2ca0968314c91",
          "text": "When working inside a worktree, write every path you show me relative to the main checkout, not the worktree root \u2014 prefix it with the worktree's own directory (e.g. `.worktrees/<name>/\u2026`). I am standing in the main checkout, where a worktree-relative path does not resolve."
        },
        {
          "id": "clause:3ec3c0ef00e24fa9b7f76f18154a895d",
          "offset": 281,
          "overlaps": [],
          "parent_sha256": "9181921d4a1e05c3a62083c6243b1fdc8ab65446b6eabc52d2f73aaea1fd9394",
          "sha256": "9a6979a47f688e0428f639b84251ef6fe74fbc1173a0a9245e9f4cd70903cd07",
          "text": "Inside a worktree the real path is in the host's storage (git and `pwd -P` show it); still write `.worktrees/<name>/\u2026`, by convention, not by reading the cwd."
        }
      ],
      "locator": {
        "kind": "git",
        "owner": "lore",
        "path": "instructions/fragments/git.md",
        "reference": "Public policy text before marker-only migration; identity bound by exact text hash.",
